age of Black's king position and creates concrete threats.\n\n**Reason:** Black's king moved early to f7, creating a positional weakness. Bc4 develops actively while exploiting this by aiming directly at the king, creating immediate tactical pressure that Black must address. This is more forcing than slow central expansion.\n\n**Answer:** B: f1-c4"}
