his is more forcing than e6 and creates better long-term pressure.\n\nReason: The move Bd5 centralizes my bishop on the most powerful square available, directly pressuring Black's exposed king on f7 and controlling critical central squares. This forces Black into a defensive posture while I maintain the initiative. The bishop is well-placed for both attack and defense from d5.\n\nAnswer: B: c4-d5"}
