----+----+----+----+\n     a    b    c    d    e    f    g    h \nYour valid moves are (src-dst-promotion, or src-dst):\n[K: e1-d1, K: e1-e2, K: e1-f1]\nYour answer format should be: Answer: piece-name: move. \nPiece-name and move (src-dst-promotion or src-dst) should be directly copied EXACTLY from valid move list.\nExample of valid output format: N: a1-b3; P: e7-e8-q; Piece B: g5-f4.\nPlease select a move from your valid moves that maximize your probability of winning.\n', 'reasoning': '', 'output': "Looking at this position, I need to assess the situation carefully.\n\n**Evaluation:**\n\nCurrent position analysis:\n- My king on e1 is severely restricted with only 3 legal moves\n- Black has a dangerous knight on c2, which is attacking key squares and contributing to my king's confinement\n- Black's king on f7 has moved and appears relatively active\n- Material seems roughly balanced, but my position is cramped\n- The knight on c2 is deep in my position and threatening\n\nLet me evaluate the three king moves:\n\n1. **K: e1-d1** - Moves toward the queenside, closer to the Black knight on c2. This seems passive and doesn't improve my king safety.\n\n2. **K: e1-e2** - Moves forward one square. This centralizes the king slightly and keeps more options open. However, it exposes the king more in the center.\n\n3. **K: e1-f1** - Moves toward the kingside, away from the immediate threats. This allows potential rook activation via h1 and keeps the king relatively safer on the back rank.\n\nGiven that I have a rook on h1 that hasn't moved, moving the king to f1 opens up potential for the h-file rook to become more active. It also distances my king from the troublesome knight on c2.\n\n**Reason:**\n\nI choose K: e1-f1 because:\n- It moves my king away from the Black knight on c2 which is creating threats\n- It maintains king safety on the back rank\n- It potentially allows my h1 rook to activate along the h-file or g-file in future moves\n- It's the most flexible move that doesn't worsen my position\n\n**Answer: K: e1-f1**"}
